 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "West Wind, bring to us a delicate wind\nFrom the boundless deeps of the ages behind,\nAnd breathe it upon the arid desert\nWhere the dust and the naked dirt\nAre like mountains sleeping upon\nThe never-waning summer night; our\nSedentary hearts shall forget\nTheir own solitude: wherever\nWe walk in many, with those who follow\nBut who know not yet whom we wander\nUpon the deserted highway\nOf hope, and what will remain",
